abstract: >-
  pLCA-NEST is an open-source Python tool that couples a prospective life cycle
  assessment (pLCA) of the final energy use of urban building stocks, assessed
  building by building, with a multiple criteria decision analysis (MCDA)
  ranking of alternative scenarios. The ecoinvent background database is
  regenerated with premise from integrated assessment model (IAM) scenarios,
  such as those of REMIND, for a reference year chosen by the user, and the
  calculations are performed with brightway. Fifteen EN 15804+A2 impact
  categories, characterised with the Environmental Footprint (EF) 3.1 impact
  assessment methods, are reported, eleven of which enter the ranking as
  criteria. The ranking combines objective weights from the modified
  indifference threshold-based attribute ratio analysis (m-ITARA) and subjective
  weights from a trigonometric fuzzy Ordinal Priority Approach (OPA) through an
  evidence-weighted convex synthesis (EWCS), and orders the scenarios with the
  fuzzy Bonferroni CoCoSo method. In its LCA part, pLCA-NEST is based on the
  structure of the LCA4DHC tool (Autelitano and Famiglietti, 2026), developed by
  the Politecnico di Milano unit of NEST Task 8.5.2, adapted to prospective LCA,
  to a different object (each building of an urban stock rather than a district
  heating and cooling network) and to different functional units.
keywords:
  - prospective life cycle assessment
  - LCA
  - urban energy systems
  - building stock
  - neighbourhood
  - MCDA
  - multiple criteria decision analysis
  - fuzzy OPA
  - CoCoSo
  - premise
  - brightway
